[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bring CI up to par before this branch merges, not while proving it out

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-CI-UP-TO-PAR-BEFORE-MERGE
TITLE: Bring CI up to par before this branch merges, not while proving it out
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
CI is required to merge, so this branch cannot land without it. The operator's
position for now is deliberately the other way round: additional CI tooling is
not required for the bulk of this experiment, because the point is to prove the
approach out before investing in machinery around it.

So: existing CI tooling is fine, and an agent that adds tooling without having
got that memo is also fine -- neither is worth reverting. What is needed is a
pass before merge that checks what actually gates the branch, rather than
discovering at restack time that the gates were never wired.

Do this when the long-lived branch is restacked into reviewable pull requests,
not before.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Recorded because "CI is not required" and "CI is required to merge" are both
true at different times, and only writing the second one down keeps the first
from being read as permanent.
<<<
